  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Module 5 - Investment Returns</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>An investor makes an initial investment of KES \({@v0@}\). After \({@n@}\) years, the value of the investment has grown to KES \({@vn@}\).</p>
<p>Calculate the following measures of return:</p>
<p>1. <strong>Absolute Return</strong> (in KES): [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>2. <strong>Relative Return</strong> (as a percentage, e.g., enter 20 for 20%): [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>3. <strong>Annualized Return</strong> (as a percentage, to 2 decimal places): [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p><strong>1. Absolute Return:</strong></p>
<p>\[ \text{Absolute Return} = \text{Ending Value} - \text{Beginning Value} \]</p>
<p>\[ = {@vn@} - {@v0@} = {@ta1@} \text{ KES} \]</p>

<p><strong>2. Relative Return:</strong></p>
<p>\[ \text{Relative Return (\%)} = \left( \frac{\text{Ending Value} - \text{Beginning Value}}{\text{Beginning Value}} \right) \times 100 \]</p>
<p>\[ = \left( \frac{{@vn@} - {@v0@}}{{@v0@}} \right) \times 100 = \frac{{@ta1@}}{{@v0@}} \times 100 = {@ta2@}\% \]</p>

<p><strong>3. Annualized Return:</strong></p>
<p>\[ \text{Annualized Return} = \left[ \left( \frac{\text{Ending Value}}{\text{Beginning Value}} \right)^{1/n} - 1 \right] \times 100 \]</p>
<p>\[ = \left[ \left( \frac{{@vn@}}{{@v0@}} \right)^{1/{@n@}} - 1 \right] \times 100 \]</p>
<p>\[ = [ {@ratio@}^{@1/n@} - 1 ] \times 100 \]</p>
<p>\[ \approx {@ta3@}\% \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber></idnumber>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025073100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>v0: 100 * (rand(9)+1); /* 100 to 900 */
growth: rand(50)+20; /* 20% to 69% growth */
vn: v0 * (1 + growth/100);
n: rand(3)+2; /* 2 to 4 years */
ta1: vn - v0;
ta2: ((vn - v0)/v0) * 100;
ratio: vn/v0;
ta3: (ratio^(1/n) - 1) * 100;
</text>
    </questionvariables>
