<!-- question: 169586 -->
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Module 5 - Portfolio Analysis</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Consider a portfolio consisting of two stocks, A and B, with equal allocation (50% each).</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Stock A:</strong> Return = \({@rA@}\%\), Beta = \({@betaA@}\)</li>
<li><strong>Stock B:</strong> Return = \({@rB@}\%\), Beta = \({@betaB@}\)</li>
</ul>
<p>The risk-free rate is \({@rf@}\%\) and the portfolio standard deviation is \({@sigmaP@}\%\).</p>
<p>Calculate the following:</p>
<p>1. <strong>Portfolio Return</strong> (%): [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>2. <strong>Portfolio Beta</strong>: [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>3. <strong>Sharpe Ratio</strong> (to 3 decimal places): [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p><strong>1. Portfolio Return (\(R_p\)):</strong></p>
<p>\[ R_p = w_A R_A + w_B R_B \]</p>
<p>\[ = 0.5({@rA@}) + 0.5({@rB@}) = {@ta1@}\% \]</p>

<p><strong>2. Portfolio Beta (\(\beta_p\)):</strong></p>
<p>\[ \beta_p = w_A \beta_A + w_B \beta_B \]</p>
<p>\[ = 0.5({@betaA@}) + 0.5({@betaB@}) = {@ta2@} \]</p>

<p><strong>3. Sharpe Ratio:</strong></p>
<p>\[ \text{Sharpe Ratio} = \frac{R_p - R_f}{\sigma_p} \]</p>
<p>\[ = \frac{{@ta1@} - {@rf@}}{{@sigmaP@}} \]</p>
<p>Note: We use the percentage values directly (e.g., 12 - 5 = 7) or decimals (0.12 - 0.05 = 0.07). The ratio is the same.</p>
<p>\[ = \frac{{@ta1 - rf@}}{{@sigmaP@}} = {@ta3@} \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber></idnumber>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025073100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>rA: rand(6)+10; /* 10 to 15 */
rB: rand(6)+5; /* 5 to 10 */
betaA: (rand(5)+10)/10; /* 1.0 to 1.4 */
betaB: (rand(5)+6)/10; /* 0.6 to 1.0 */
rf: rand(3)+3; /* 3 to 5 */
sigmaP: rand(4)+5; /* 5 to 8 */
ta1: 0.5*rA + 0.5*rB;
ta2: 0.5*betaA + 0.5*betaB;
ta3: (ta1 - rf)/sigmaP;
</text>
    </questionvariables>
    <specificfeedback format="html">
